📗
  Range, an immutable sequence of numbers. [Read more in the
  language reference.](../../reference/the-s-package.html#-ranges)
📗
🌍 🕊 ⏩ 🍇
  🐊 🔂🐚🔢🍆
  🐊 🐽️🐚🔢🍆

  🖍🆕 start 🔢
  🖍🆕 stop 🔢
  🖍🆕 step 🔢

  📗
    Creates a range of the integers from *start* up to, but not including,
    *stop*. The range is empty if *stop* is not greater than *start*; to count
    down, provide a negative step.
  📗
  🥯🆕 🍼 start 🔢 🍼 stop 🔢 🍇
    1 ➡️ 🖍step
  🍉
  📗
    Creates a range from *start* to *stop* with the provided *step*.
  📗
  🥯🆕 🍼 start 🔢 🍼 stop 🔢 🍼 step 🔢 🍇🍉

  📗
    Returns the *n*th element of the range, `start + step * n`. *n* is only
    valid if that is `>= start` and `< stop` (or `<= start` and `> stop` if
    *step* is negative). If *n* is invalid, the program will panic.
  📗
  ❗️ 🐽 n 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 🍇
    start ➕ n ✖️ step ➡️ v
    ↪️ step ◀️ 0 🍇
      ↪️ stop ◀️ v 🤝 v ◀️🙌 start 🍇
        ↩️ v
      🍉
    🍉
    🙅 🍇
      ↪️ start ◀️🙌 v 🤝 v ◀️ stop 🍇
        ↩️ v
      🍉
    🍉
    🤯🐇💻 🔤Index out of bounds in ⏩🐽❗️🔤 ❗️
    ↩️ 0
  🍉

  📗 Returns the number of integers in this range. 📗
  ❓ 📏 ➡️ 🔢 🍇
    ↪️ step ◀️ 0 🍇
      ↪️ stop ▶️🙌 start 🍇
        ↩️ 0
      🍉
      ↩️ 🤜stop ➖ start ➕ step ➕ 1🤛 ➗ step
    🍉
    ↪️ stop ◀️🙌 start 🍇
      ↩️ 0
    🍉
    ↩️ 🤜stop ➖ start ➕ step ➖ 1🤛 ➗ step
  🍉

  📗 Returns an iterator to iterate over integers in this range. 📗
  ❗️ 🍡 ➡️ 👣 🍇
    ↩️ 🆕👣 start step 📏👇❓❗️
  🍉
🍉

📗
  Iterator over a [[⏩]].

  Being a value type whose methods are inlined, iterating a range with 🔂
  compiles to a plain counting loop. Like other values, a copy of an iterator
  is independent of it: iterating one copy does not advance the others.
📗
